<title>HONG KONG: No &quot;political pressure&quot; for deal - HK Tel.</title>
<headline>No &quot;political pressure&quot; for deal - HK Tel.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong Telecommunications Ltd said on Friday it and Cable &amp; Wireless Plc were under no &quot;political pressure&quot; from China for any deal.  </p>
<p>Speaking at a news conference in Hong Kong after C&amp;W announced it would sell 5.5 percent of Hongkong Telecom to state-owned China Telecom, Hongkong Telecom chief executive Linus Cheung said there had been no &quot;political pressure&quot; from Beijing for a deal.</p>
<p>Cheung is also a member of C&amp;W's board.</p>
<p>C&amp;W said it would sell the stake in Hongkong Telecom for HK$14.25 per share in a deal worth a total of 726 million stg.</p>
<p>C&amp;W owned about 59 percent of Hongkong Telecom prior to the deal.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441  http://www.hk97.com</p>
